"hand.kfx: tier 2's machine (C126), Fixpt's `fx-cells-asminterp`: the
 cellular words tier 1 runs, run by arm64 routines this file emits with
 FX-26's own encoder (`fx26:arm64.fx`), placed by `seal-code` and called
 as a native procedure (C116). It runs on tier 1's memory as it is,
 shared (C126): the heap, the two stacks and its registers, KFX flat
 arrays given to it as Fixpt's flat arrays. A cell it has no routine for,
 or whose checks do not all pass, it gives back before changing anything,
 for tier 1 to run as ever (machine.kfx's `step!`); then tier 1 enters it
 again. So it agrees with tier 1 from its first routine, each step
 counted as tier 1 counts it.

 Its registers: the heap's base, the ip (the address of the next cell),
 `cur`, the data stack's top and the return stack's (addresses of the next
 free element), the state's address, the data stack's base, the frame
 (an address), `clo`, the fuel, and the cell being run (for giving back).
 Unlike Fixpt's, the stacks grow up, as tier 1's do.
 fixpt-source: crates/fixpt-native/src/cellular.rs@8c7111d"

(define a64 (load-input "fx26:arm64.fx"))

"Registers."
(define x-mem int 19)
(define x-ip int 20)
(define x-cur int 21)
(define x-dsp int 22)
(define x-rsp int 23)
(define x-st int 24)
(define x-dsb int 25)
(define x-fp int 26)
(define x-clo int 27)
(define x-fuel int 28)
(define x-cell int 12)
(define x-w int 9)
(define x10 int 10)
(define x11 int 11)
(define x13 int 13)
(define x14 int 14)
(define x15 int 15)
(define x16 int 16)
(define x17 int 17)

"Conditions, as `arm64.fx` numbers them."
(define c-eq int 0)
(define c-ne int 1)
(define c-hs int 2)
(define c-lo int 3)
(define c-vs int 6)
(define c-hi int 8)
(define c-ls int 9)
(define c-lt int 11)

"The state, a flat array of `i64`, by element: what tier 1 gives the
 machine and takes back (`cur`, `kk`, `fp`, `clo`, `dsp`, `rsp`, `fuel`),
 why the machine stopped, the limits as tier 1 checks them, the heap's
 `top`, the most it may be at an allocation before tier 1 would collect
 (0 under `--gc-stress`), the heap's length, and what the
 machine works out from them at its entry: the return stack's base, and
 the limits as addresses."
(define st-cur int 0)
(define st-kk int 1)
(define st-fp int 2)
(define st-clo int 3)
(define st-dsp int 4)
(define st-rsp int 5)
(define st-fuel int 6)
(define st-ds-limit int 8)
(define st-rs-limit int 9)
(define st-ds-length int 10)
(define st-rs-push int 11)
(define st-rsb int 12)
(define st-ds-lim int 13)
(define st-rs-lim int 14)
(define st-ds-end int 15)
(define st-rs-end int 16)
(define st-top int 17)
(define st-alloc-limit int 18)
(define st-mem-length int 19)
"Register code's `RESULT` and `REG1`…`REG8` (C130), in `x0`…`x8` while the
 machine runs, as Fixpt's tier 5 keeps them."
(define st-regs int 20)
"Where the code starts (C131): its tables are at fixed places past it."
(define st-start int 29)
"The values' base (C139): the heap's address, the values being
 addresses, or 0 (`--indexes`); the machine's base register is the heap's
 address less it, so that a value plus it is the value's word."
(define st-vbase int 34)
"Its length: 30 to 32 are hand-x64.kfx's own, 33 tier 6's (`st-t6link`)."
(define st-size i64 35)
(define at-st (->* (int) int) (lambda (i) (* 8 i)))

"Why the machine stopped: to give a cell back; or the return stack ran
 out under its entries' marks, which tier 1 would read past."
(define gave-back i64 1)
(define ran-out i64 2)
(define misaligned i64 3)

"Code: instructions, and jumps to labels, placed when every label is."
(define-datatype item (ins int) (jump int int int) (label-here int) (offset-of int) (align-odd int))
(define j-b int 0)
(define j-cond int 1)
(define j-cbz int 2)
(define j-adr int 3)
(define j-cbnz int 4)
(define j-bl int 5)
"A `nop`, and `align-odd!`: one if the next instruction's place is even,
 so that the one after it, where a `blr` returns, is 8-aligned (C131)."
(define arm-nop int 3573751839)

(define hand-items (ref (listof item @c) @c) (new nil))
"Data, placed before the code: 8 bytes an entry."
(define hand-data (ref (listof item @c) @c) (new nil))
(define hand-labels (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define e! (->* (int) unit) (lambda (w) (set hand-items (cons (ins w) (get hand-items)))))
(define label! (->* () int) (lambda () (let ((l (get hand-labels))) (begin (set hand-labels (+ l 1)) l))))
(define bind! (->* (int) unit) (lambda (l) (set hand-items (cons (label-here l) (get hand-items)))))
(define b! (->* (int) unit) (lambda (l) (set hand-items (cons (jump j-b 0 l) (get hand-items)))))
(define bc! (->* (int int) unit) (lambda (c l) (set hand-items (cons (jump j-cond c l) (get hand-items)))))
(define cbz! (->* (int int) unit) (lambda (r l) (set hand-items (cons (jump j-cbz r l) (get hand-items)))))
(define adr! (->* (int int) unit) (lambda (r l) (set hand-items (cons (jump j-adr r l) (get hand-items)))))
(define bl! (->* (int) unit) (lambda (l) (set hand-items (cons (jump j-bl 0 l) (get hand-items)))))
(define align-odd! (->* () unit) (lambda () (set hand-items (cons (align-odd 0) (get hand-items)))))
(define d! (->* (item) unit) (lambda (i) (set hand-data (cons (ins 0) (cons i (get hand-data))))))
(define data-label! (->* (int) unit) (lambda (l) (set hand-data (cons (label-here l) (get hand-data)))))

"`adr xd, label`, which `arm64.fx` has not: a byte offset of 21 bits."
(define arm-adr (->* (int int) int)
  (lambda (d bytes)
    (let ((v (modulo bytes 2097152)))
      (+ 268435456 (+ (* (modulo v 4) 536870912) (+ (* (quotient v 4) 32) d))))))

(define-rec
  (placed! (->* ((listof item @c) int (flatarrayof i64 @c)) int)
    (lambda (xs at ls)
      "Each label's place, in instructions, in `ls`; how many there are."
      (if (null? xs)
          at
          (tagcase (car xs)
            (ins (w) (placed! (cdr xs) (+ at 1) ls))
            (jump (k a l) (placed! (cdr xs) (+ at 1) ls))
            (offset-of (l) (placed! (cdr xs) (+ at 1) ls))
            (align-odd (z) (placed! (cdr xs) (if (= (modulo at 2) 0) (+ at 1) at) ls))
            (label-here (l) (begin (flatarray-set-i64! ls (int->i64 l) (int->i64 at)) (placed! (cdr xs) at ls))))))))

(define where (->* ((flatarrayof i64 @c) int) int) (lambda (ls l) (i64->int (flatarray-ref-i64 ls (int->i64 l)))))

(define encoded (->* (item int (flatarrayof i64 @c)) int)
  (lambda (x at ls)
    "Item `x`, at `at`, encoded; a jump to where its label is, an offset
     its label's in bytes."
    (tagcase x
      (ins (w) w)
      (jump (k a l)
        (let ((d (- (where ls l) at)))
          (cond ((= k j-b) ((with a64 arm-b) d))
                ((= k j-cond) ((with a64 arm-b-cond) a d))
                ((= k j-cbz) ((with a64 arm-cbz) a d))
                ((= k j-cbnz) ((with a64 arm-cbnz) a d))
                ((= k j-bl) ((with a64 arm-bl) d))
                (else (arm-adr a (* 4 d))))))
      (offset-of (l) (* 4 (where ls l)))
      (align-odd (z) arm-nop)
      (label-here (l) 0))))

"Instructions, by `arm64.fx`'s encoders."
(define ldr! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (t n o) (e! ((with a64 arm-ldr) t n o))))
(define str! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (t n o) (e! ((with a64 arm-str) t n o))))
(define ldur! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (t n o) (e! ((with a64 arm-ldur) t n o))))
(define stur! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (t n o) (e! ((with a64 arm-stur) t n o))))
(define ldr-post! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (t n o) (e! ((with a64 arm-ldr-post) t n o))))
(define str-post! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (t n o) (e! ((with a64 arm-str-post) t n o))))
(define add! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n m) (e! ((with a64 arm-add) d n m))))
(define sub! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n m) (e! ((with a64 arm-sub) d n m))))
(define adds! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n m) (e! ((with a64 arm-adds) d n m))))
(define subs! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n m) (e! ((with a64 arm-subs) d n m))))
(define addi! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n i) (e! ((with a64 arm-add-imm) d n i))))
(define subi! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n i) (e! ((with a64 arm-sub-imm) d n i))))
(define cmp! (->* (int int) unit) (lambda (n m) (e! ((with a64 arm-cmp) n m))))
(define cmpi! (->* (int int) unit) (lambda (n i) (e! ((with a64 arm-cmp-imm) n i))))
(define mov! (->* (int int) unit) (lambda (d m) (e! ((with a64 arm-mov) d m))))
(define movz! (->* (int int) unit) (lambda (d i) (e! ((with a64 arm-movz) d i 0))))
(define orr! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n m) (e! ((with a64 arm-orr) d n m))))
(define andl! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n bits) (e! ((with a64 arm-and-low) d n bits))))
(define tstl! (->* (int int) unit) (lambda (n bits) (e! ((with a64 arm-tst-low) n bits))))
(define asr! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n s) (e! ((with a64 arm-asr-imm) d n s))))
(define lsr! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n s) (e! ((with a64 arm-lsr-imm) d n s))))
(define csel! (->* (int int int int) unit) (lambda (d n m c) (e! ((with a64 arm-csel) d n m c))))
(define br! (->* (int) unit) (lambda (n) (e! ((with a64 arm-br) n))))
(define blr! (->* (int) unit) (lambda (n) (e! ((with a64 arm-blr) n))))
(define stp-pre! (->* (int int int int) unit) (lambda (t t2 n i) (e! ((with a64 arm-stp-pre) t t2 n i))))
(define ldp-post! (->* (int int int int) unit) (lambda (t t2 n i) (e! ((with a64 arm-ldp-post) t t2 n i))))
(define stp! (->* (int int int int) unit) (lambda (t t2 n i) (e! ((with a64 arm-stp) t t2 n i))))
(define ldp! (->* (int int int int) unit) (lambda (t t2 n i) (e! ((with a64 arm-ldp) t t2 n i))))
(define ubfx! (->* (int int int int) unit) (lambda (d n lsb w) (e! ((with a64 arm-ubfx) d n lsb w))))
"`lsl xd, xn, #s`, which `arm64.fx` has not: `ubfm` of `64 - s`, `63 - s`."
(define arm-lsl (->* (int int int) int)
  (lambda (d n sh) (+ 3544186880 (+ (* (modulo (- 64 sh) 64) 65536) (+ (* (- 63 sh) 1024) (+ (* n 32) d))))))
(define lsl! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n sh) (e! (arm-lsl d n sh))))
"`mul` and `smulh`, which `arm64.fx` has not: `madd xd, xn, xm, xzr`, and
 the high 64 bits of the signed product."
(define mul! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n m) (e! (+ 2600500224 (+ (* m 65536) (+ (* n 32) d))))))
(define smulh! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n m) (e! (+ 2604694528 (+ (* m 65536) (+ (* n 32) d))))))
(define ret! (->* () unit) (lambda () (e! (with a64 arm-ret))))
(define ldr-reg! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (t n m) (e! ((with a64 arm-ldr-reg) t n m))))

(define times8! (->* (int) unit)
  (lambda (r) "`r` times 8." (begin (add! r r r) (add! r r r) (add! r r r))))

"The labels every routine shares."
(define l-next (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define l-give (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define l-give-pre (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define l-ran-out (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define l-pop-return (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define l-resume (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define l-resume-give (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define l-misaligned (ref int @c) (new 0))
"Where the code starts, where the machine is entered, and where the
 table of the compiled words' tables of where to resume is (C128)."
(define l-start (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define l-entry (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define l-words (ref int @c) (new 0))

"Compiling a word (tier 4, C128): the label of the next cell's code, and
 of a branch's target's; -1 in the machine, or for a target not compiled."
(define h-cont (ref int @c) (new -1))
(define h-target (ref int @c) (new -1))

(define give-if! (->* (int) unit) (lambda (c) "Give the cell back if `c`." (bc! c (get l-give))))
(define next! (->* () unit)
  (lambda () "On to the next cell." (b! (if (< (get h-cont) 0) (get l-next) (get h-cont)))))
(define taken! (->* () unit)
  (lambda () "On to a branch's target, the ip moved to it." (b! (if (< (get h-target) 0) (get l-next) (get h-target)))))
(define resume! (->* () unit)
  (lambda () "On to the cell at the ip, of `cur`: its code if it has some." (b! (get l-resume))))

(define need! (->* (int) unit)
  (lambda (n)
    "At least `n` values on the data stack (1 or 2), else give back: tier 1
     traps there, finding too few."
    (if (= n 1)
        (begin (cmp! x-dsp x-dsb) (give-if! c-ls))
        (begin (addi! x13 x-dsb 8) (cmp! x-dsp x13) (give-if! c-ls)))))

(define h-room! (->* () unit)
  (lambda ()
    "Room to push one, else give back (tier 1's `push!` traps)."
    (begin (ldr! x16 x-st (at-st st-ds-end)) (cmp! x-dsp x16) (give-if! c-hs))))

(define limits! (->* () unit)
  (lambda ()
    "Within the limits tier 1's `check-limits!` holds to, else give back."
    (begin
      (ldr! x16 x-st (at-st st-ds-lim)) (cmp! x-dsp x16) (give-if! c-hi)
      (ldr! x16 x-st (at-st st-rs-lim)) (cmp! x-rsp x16) (give-if! c-hs))))

(define put-top! (->* (int) unit)
  (lambda (r) "Two values replaced by `r`." (begin (subi! x-dsp x-dsp 8) (stur! r x-dsp -8) (next!))))

(define boolean-of! (->* (int) unit)
  (lambda (c) "`x13` := `#t` if `c`, else `#f`." (begin (movz! x13 11) (movz! x14 3) (csel! x13 x13 x14 c))))

(define two-fixnums! (->* () unit)
  (lambda ()
    "`x13` the one below the top, `x14` the top; both fixnums, else give back."
    (begin (need! 2) (ldur! x13 x-dsp -16) (ldur! x14 x-dsp -8) (orr! x15 x13 x14) (tstl! x15 3) (give-if! c-ne))))

(define kind-in! (->* (int i64) unit)
  (lambda (r kind)
    "`x11` the heap's address of the value in `r` plus 4; given back unless
     it is a bloblet with a trailer whose header says `kind` (Fixpt's
     `is_closure`)."
    (begin
      (andl! x13 r 3) (cmpi! x13 4) (give-if! c-ne)
      (add! x11 x-mem r) (ldur! x15 x11 -12) (andl! x13 x15 3) (cmpi! x13 5) (give-if! c-ne)
      (sub! x14 x11 x15) (ldur! x14 x14 -7) (ubfx! x14 x14 3 8) (cmpi! x14 (i64->int kind)) (give-if! c-ne))))

(define closure-in! (->* (int) unit)
  (lambda (r) "`kind-in!`, of a cellular closure." (kind-in! r k-closure)))


(define-rec
  (regs-zeroed! (->* (int) unit)
    (lambda (r)
      "`xr`… to `x8` 0: dead registers harmless when spilled (machine.kfx's
       `regs-cleared!`)."
      (if (> r 8) #u (begin (mov! r 31) (regs-zeroed! (+ r 1)))))))

(define-rec
  (args-loaded! (->* (int int) unit)
    (lambda (r loaded)
      "`xr`… from the frame, as many as the count in `x17` (times 8)."
      (if (> r 8)
          #u
          (begin (cmpi! x17 (* 8 r)) (bc! c-lo loaded) (ldr! r x-fp (* 8 (- r 1))) (args-loaded! (+ r 1) loaded))))))

(define h-adapted! (->* () unit)
  (lambda ()
    "A call of a word whose twin is register code of as many arguments
     (`--regs`, C129), entered as tier 1's `call!` enters it: the frame's
     values into `x1`…, the frame dropped, the register word at its first
     instruction past `args`. `x17` the count, times 8."
    (let ((done (label!)) (loaded (label!)))
      (begin
        (add! x14 x-mem x-cur) (ldur! x13 x14 (- -4 (* 8 (i64->int f-twin)))) (cmpi! x13 3) (bc! c-eq done)
        (add! x14 x-mem x13) (ldur! x15 x14 (- -4 (* 8 (+ (i64->int f-cell0) 1)))) (cmp! x15 x17) (bc! c-ne done)
        (regs-zeroed! 0)
        (args-loaded! 1 loaded)
        (bind! loaded)
        (mov! x-dsp x-fp) (mov! x-cur x13)
        (add! x-ip x-mem x-cur) (subi! x-ip x-ip (+ 4 (* 8 (+ (i64->int f-cell0) 2))))
        (bind! done)))))

(define called! (->* (bool) unit)
  (lambda (tail)
    "A call of the closure on top with the `count` values below it (tier
     1's `call!`), in tail position its frame slid down over this one's;
     the count, times 8, in `x17`, which `closure-in!` keeps."
    (let ((loop (label!)) (done (label!)))
      (begin
        (ldr-post! x17 x-ip -8)
        (add! x14 x-fp x17) (addi! x14 x14 8) (cmp! x-dsp x14) (give-if! c-lo)
        (ldur! x10 x-dsp -8)
        (closure-in! x10)
        (limits!)
        (if tail
            (begin
              (subi! x14 x-dsp 8) (sub! x15 x14 x17) (mov! x16 x-fp)
              (bind! loop) (cmp! x15 x14) (bc! c-hs done)
              (ldr-post! x-w x15 8) (str-post! x-w x16 8) (b! loop)
              (bind! done) (add! x-dsp x-fp x17))
            (begin
              (ldr! x16 x-st (at-st st-rs-end)) (cmp! x-rsp x16) (give-if! c-hs)
              (add! x14 x-mem x-cur) (subi! x14 x14 4) (sub! x14 x14 x-ip)
              (sub! x15 x-fp x-dsb)
              (stp! x-cur x14 x-rsp 0) (stp! x15 x-clo x-rsp 16) (addi! x-rsp x-rsp 32)
              (subi! x-dsp x-dsp 8) (sub! x-fp x-dsp x17)))
        (ldur! x-cur x11 (- -4 (* 8 (i64->int f-word))))
        (mov! x-clo x10)
        (add! x-ip x-mem x-cur) (subi! x-ip x-ip (+ 4 (* 8 (i64->int f-cell0))))
        (h-adapted!)
        (resume!)))))



(define fields-of! (->* (int) unit)
  (lambda (lowest)
    "`x15` eight times the fields of the bloblet whose address plus 4 is in
     `x11`, `x14` eight times the lowest that may be read: past a trailer,
     its distance, 2; past a header, its count, 1; else given back."
    (let ((header (label!)) (done (label!)))
      (begin
        (ldur! x15 x11 -12) (andl! x14 x15 3) (cmpi! x14 5) (bc! c-ne header)
        (subi! x15 x15 5) (movz! x14 16) (b! done)
        (bind! header)
        (cmpi! x14 6) (give-if! c-ne)
        (ubfx! x15 x15 14 18) (times8! x15) (movz! x14 8)
        (bind! done)))))

(define field-read! (->* () unit)
  (lambda ()
    "`x16` field `x13 / 8` of the bloblet at `x11`, if it may be read (tier
     1's `field-ok?`), else given back."
    (begin
      (fields-of! 0)
      (cmp! x13 x14) (give-if! c-lt) (cmp! x13 x15) (give-if! c-hi)
      (sub! x16 x11 x13) (ldur! x16 x16 -4))))

(define allocating! (->* (int int) unit)
  (lambda (words count8)
    "Room for an object of `words` words more than `count8 / 8` (`count8`
     a register, or 31 for none): `x13` the heap's `top`, `x16` its
     address. Given back if tier 1's `safepoint!` would collect first, or
     `room!` grow the heap."
    (begin
      (ldr! x13 x-st (at-st st-top)) (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-alloc-limit)) (cmp! x13 x14) (give-if! c-hi)
      (addi! x15 x13 words)
      (if (= count8 31) #u (begin (lsr! x14 count8 3) (add! x15 x15 x14)))
      (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-mem-length)) (cmp! x15 x14) (give-if! c-hi)
      (lsl! x16 x13 3) (add! x16 x-mem x16) (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-vbase)) (add! x16 x16 x14))))

(define consed! (->* (bool) unit)
  (lambda (region)
    "`cons`, or `%region-cons` (its region below the two, and dropped):
     the pair at the heap's top, as tier 1's `cons!` makes it."
    (begin
      (if region (begin (addi! x13 x-dsb 24) (cmp! x-dsp x13) (give-if! c-lo)) (need! 2))
      (allocating! 2 31)
      (ldur! x14 x-dsp -16) (ldur! x15 x-dsp -8) (stp! x14 x15 x16 0)
      (addi! x15 x13 2) (str! x15 x-st (at-st st-top))
      (if region (subi! x-dsp x-dsp 8) #u)
      (sub! x14 x16 x-mem) (addi! x14 x14 1) (put-top! x14))))

(define primed! (->* () unit)
  (lambda ()
    "`prim P COUNT`: those primitives the machine has, else given back.
     `P`'s op is above its 16 bits of arity (prims.kfx's `prim-op`); the
     count has been checked against the arity when it is the arity's one."
    (let ((region-cons (label!)))
      (begin
        (ldr-post! x13 x-ip -8) (ldr-post! x17 x-ip -8)
        (lsr! x14 x13 19)
        (cmpi! x14 (i64->int o-region-cons)) (bc! c-eq region-cons)
        (b! (get l-give))
        (bind! region-cons)
        (cmpi! x17 24) (give-if! c-ne)
        (consed! #t)))))

(define closed! (->* () unit)
  (lambda ()
    "`closure W COUNT`: a cellular closure of word `W` over the `COUNT`
     values on top, as tier 1's `make-bloblet!` lays it out: its header,
     its fields (`count + 2`, the trailer one), its trailer."
    (let ((loop (label!)) (done (label!)))
      (begin
        (h-room!)
        (ldr-post! x10 x-ip -8) (ldr-post! x17 x-ip -8)
        (add! x14 x-fp x17) (cmp! x-dsp x14) (give-if! c-lo)
        (allocating! 3 x17)
        (movz! x15 (+ 6 (* 8 (i64->int k-closure)))) (lsr! x14 x17 3) (addi! x14 x14 2) (lsl! x14 x14 14) (orr! x15 x15 x14)
        (str! x15 x16 0)
        (add! x11 x16 x17) (addi! x11 x11 24)
        (addi! x14 x17 21) (stur! x14 x11 -8)
        (stur! x10 x11 -16)
        (sub! x15 x-dsp x17) (subi! x-w x11 24)
        (bind! loop) (cmp! x15 x-dsp) (bc! c-hs done)
        (ldr-post! x14 x15 8) (str-post! x14 x-w -8) (b! loop)
        (bind! done)
        (sub! x-dsp x-dsp x17)
        (lsr! x14 x17 3) (add! x14 x14 x13) (addi! x14 x14 3) (str! x14 x-st (at-st st-top))
        (sub! x14 x11 x-mem) (addi! x14 x14 4) (str-post! x14 x-dsp 8)
        (next!)))))

(define word-entered! (->* () unit)
  (lambda ()
    "The word in `x9`, a cell, entered as tier 1's `enter!` does, if its
     entry is `docol` or past the routines (compiled, C128)."
    (let ((docol (label!)))
      (begin
      (andl! x13 x-w 3) (cmpi! x13 4) (give-if! c-ne)
      (add! x11 x-mem x-w)
      (ldur! x10 x11 (- -4 (* 8 (i64->int f-entry))))
      (movz! x13 (* 8 (i64->int r-docol))) (cmp! x10 x13) (bc! c-eq docol)
      (cmpi! x10 (* 8 (i64->int r-count))) (give-if! c-lo)
      (bind! docol)
      (limits!)
      (andl! x13 x-cur 3) (cmpi! x13 4) (give-if! c-ne)
      (ldr! x16 x-st (at-st st-rs-end)) (cmp! x-rsp x16) (give-if! c-hs)
      (add! x13 x-mem x-cur) (subi! x13 x13 4) (sub! x13 x13 x-ip)
      (sub! x14 x-fp x-dsb)
      (stp! x-cur x13 x-rsp 0) (stp! x14 x-clo x-rsp 16) (addi! x-rsp x-rsp 32)
      (mov! x-cur x-w)
      (subi! x-ip x11 (+ 4 (* 8 (i64->int f-cell0))))
      (resume!)))))

(define entered! (->* (int) unit)
  (lambda (n)
    "Routine number `n`'s code; what it does not do it gives back."
    (cond
      ((= n (i64->int r-lit))
       (begin (h-room!) (ldr-post! x13 x-ip -8) (str-post! x13 x-dsp 8) (next!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-dup))
       (begin (need! 1) (h-room!) (ldur! x13 x-dsp -8) (str-post! x13 x-dsp 8) (next!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-drop)) (begin (need! 1) (subi! x-dsp x-dsp 8) (next!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-swap))
       (begin (need! 2) (ldur! x13 x-dsp -8) (ldur! x14 x-dsp -16) (stur! x13 x-dsp -16) (stur! x14 x-dsp -8) (next!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-over))
       (begin (need! 2) (h-room!) (ldur! x13 x-dsp -16) (str-post! x13 x-dsp 8) (next!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-eq))
       (begin (need! 2) (ldur! x13 x-dsp -16) (ldur! x14 x-dsp -8) (cmp! x13 x14) (boolean-of! c-eq) (put-top! x13)))
      ((or (= n (i64->int r-add)) (= n (i64->int r-int-add)))
       (begin (two-fixnums!) (adds! x13 x13 x14) (give-if! c-vs) (put-top! x13)))
      ((or (= n (i64->int r-sub)) (= n (i64->int r-int-sub)))
       (begin (two-fixnums!) (subs! x13 x13 x14) (give-if! c-vs) (put-top! x13)))
      ((or (= n (i64->int r-less)) (= n (i64->int r-int-less)))
       (begin (two-fixnums!) (cmp! x13 x14) (boolean-of! c-lt) (put-top! x13)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-int-eq))
       (begin (two-fixnums!) (cmp! x13 x14) (boolean-of! c-eq) (put-top! x13)))
      ((or (= n (i64->int r-car)) (= n (i64->int r-cdr)) (= n (i64->int r-pair-car)) (= n (i64->int r-pair-cdr)))
       (begin
         (need! 1) (ldur! x13 x-dsp -8) (andl! x14 x13 3) (cmpi! x14 1) (give-if! c-ne)
         (add! x15 x-mem x13)
         (ldur! x16 x15 (if (or (= n (i64->int r-car)) (= n (i64->int r-pair-car))) -1 7))
         (stur! x16 x-dsp -8) (next!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-slot))
       (begin
         (ldr-post! x13 x-ip -8) (add! x14 x-fp x13)
         (cmp! x14 x-dsb) (give-if! c-lo) (cmp! x14 x-dsp) (give-if! c-hs)
         (h-room!) (ldr! x15 x14 0) (str-post! x15 x-dsp 8) (next!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-slot-set))
       (begin
         (need! 1) (ldr-post! x13 x-ip -8) (add! x14 x-fp x13) (subi! x15 x-dsp 8)
         (cmp! x14 x-dsb) (give-if! c-lo) (cmp! x14 x15) (give-if! c-hs)
         (ldur! x16 x-dsp -8) (str! x16 x14 0) (mov! x-dsp x15) (next!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-global))
       (begin
         (h-room!) (ldr-post! x13 x-ip -8) (add! x14 x-mem x13)
         (ldur! x15 x14 (- -4 (* 8 (i64->int f-value)))) (str-post! x15 x-dsp 8) (next!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-branch))
       (begin (limits!) (ldr-post! x13 x-ip -8) (sub! x-ip x-ip x13) (taken!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-zbranch))
       (let ((taken (label!)))
         (begin
           (need! 1) (ldur! x14 x-dsp -8) (cmpi! x14 3)
           (bc! c-eq taken)
           (subi! x-dsp x-dsp 8) (subi! x-ip x-ip 8) (next!)
           (bind! taken)
           (limits!) (subi! x-dsp x-dsp 8) (ldr-post! x13 x-ip -8) (sub! x-ip x-ip x13) (taken!))))
      ((or (= n (i64->int r-call)) (= n (i64->int r-tcall)))
       (called! #f))
      ((or (= n (i64->int r-tailcall)) (= n (i64->int r-ttailcall)))
       (called! #t))
      ((= n (i64->int r-free))
       (begin
         (h-room!) (ldr-post! x13 x-ip -8) (addi! x13 x13 (* 8 (i64->int f-free0)))
         (andl! x14 x-clo 3) (cmpi! x14 4) (give-if! c-ne) (add! x11 x-mem x-clo)
         (field-read!) (str-post! x16 x-dsp 8) (next!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-field))
       (begin
         (need! 1) (ldr-post! x13 x-ip -8) (ldur! x10 x-dsp -8)
         (andl! x14 x10 3) (cmpi! x14 4) (give-if! c-ne) (add! x11 x-mem x10)
         (field-read!) (stur! x16 x-dsp -8) (next!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-global-set))
       (begin
         (need! 1) (ldr-post! x13 x-ip -8) (add! x14 x-mem x13)
         (ldur! x15 x-dsp -8) (stur! x15 x14 (- -4 (* 8 (i64->int f-value))))
         (ldur! x16 x14 (- -4 (* 8 (i64->int f-writes)))) (addi! x16 x16 8) (stur! x16 x14 (- -4 (* 8 (i64->int f-writes))))
         (subi! x-dsp x-dsp 8) (next!)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-field-ref))
       (begin
         (need! 2) (ldur! x13 x-dsp -8) (tstl! x13 3) (give-if! c-ne)
         (ldur! x10 x-dsp -16) (andl! x14 x10 3) (cmpi! x14 4) (give-if! c-ne) (add! x11 x-mem x10)
         (field-read!) (put-top! x16)))
      ((= n (i64->int r-cons)) (consed! #f))
      ((= n (i64->int r-prim)) (primed!))
      ((= n (i64->int r-closure)) (closed!))
      ((= n (i64->int r-exit))
       (begin (ldr! x16 x-st (at-st st-rsb)) (cmp! x-rsp x16) (give-if! c-eq) (b! (get l-pop-return))))
      ((= n (i64->int r-return))
       (begin
         (need! 1) (subi! x15 x-dsp 8) (cmp! x15 x-fp) (give-if! c-lo)
         (ldr! x16 x-st (at-st st-rsb)) (cmp! x-rsp x16) (give-if! c-eq)
         (ldur! x13 x-dsp -8) (mov! x-dsp x-fp) (str-post! x13 x-dsp 8)
         (b! (get l-pop-return))))
      (else (b! (get l-give))))))

(define-rec
  (table! (->* (int int) unit)
    (lambda (n base)
      "A jump to each routine's code, by number: routine `n`'s label is
       `base + n`."
      (if (>= n (i64->int r-count)) #u (begin (b! (+ base n)) (table! (+ n 1) base))))))

(define-rec
  (routines! (->* (int int) unit)
    (lambda (n base)
      (if (>= n (i64->int r-count))
          #u
          (begin (bind! (+ base n)) (entered! n) (routines! (+ n 1) base))))))

(define-rec
  (regs-loaded! (->* (int) unit)
    (lambda (r) (if (> r 8) #u (begin (ldr! r x-st (at-st (+ st-regs r))) (regs-loaded! (+ r 1)))))))
(define-rec
  (regs-stored! (->* (int) unit)
    (lambda (r) (if (> r 8) #u (begin (str! r x-st (at-st (+ st-regs r))) (regs-stored! (+ r 1)))))))

(define entry! (->* () unit)
  (lambda ()
    "From the native convention: the state, the heap, the data stack and
     the return stack in `x1` to `x4`, each a flat array's suffix (tag 4).
     Every register the machine uses kept, as Fixpt's machine keeps them."
    (begin
      (stp-pre! 29 30 31 -96) (stp! 19 20 31 16) (stp! 21 22 31 32) (stp! 23 24 31 48) (stp! 25 26 31 64) (stp! 27 28 31 80)
      (subi! x-st 1 4) (subi! x-mem 2 4) (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-vbase)) (sub! x-mem x-mem x14)
      (subi! x-dsb 3 4) (subi! x13 4 4) (str! x13 x-st (at-st st-rsb))
      ;; The limits, as addresses.
      (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-ds-limit)) (times8! x14) (add! x14 x-dsb x14) (str! x14 x-st (at-st st-ds-lim))
      (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-rs-limit)) (times8! x14) (add! x14 x13 x14) (str! x14 x-st (at-st st-rs-lim))
      (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-ds-length)) (times8! x14) (add! x14 x-dsb x14) (str! x14 x-st (at-st st-ds-end))
      (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-rs-push)) (times8! x14) (add! x14 x13 x14) (str! x14 x-st (at-st st-rs-end))
      ;; The registers.
      (ldr! x-cur x-st (at-st st-cur))
      (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-kk)) (times8! x14) (add! x-ip x-mem x-cur) (subi! x-ip x-ip 4) (sub! x-ip x-ip x14)
      (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-fp)) (times8! x14) (add! x-fp x-dsb x14)
      (ldr! x-clo x-st (at-st st-clo))
      (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-dsp)) (times8! x14) (add! x-dsp x-dsb x14)
      (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-rsp)) (times8! x14) (add! x-rsp x13 x14)
      (ldr! x-fuel x-st (at-st st-fuel))
      ;; The code 16-byte aligned, as kayak-jit seals it (C131: links in
      ;; frames are fixnums), else out at once.
      (adr! x16 (get l-start)) (str! x16 x-st (at-st st-start))
      (regs-loaded! 0)
      (ldr! x16 x-st (at-st st-start)) (tstl! x16 4) (bc! c-ne (get l-misaligned))
      (resume!))))

(define leave! (->* (i64) unit)
  (lambda (why)
    "The registers back in the state, the cell being run `kk`'s, and out,
     with `why`, a fixnum."
    (begin
      (regs-stored! 0)
      (str! x-cur x-st (at-st st-cur))
      (add! x13 x-mem x-cur) (subi! x13 x13 4) (sub! x13 x13 x-cell) (asr! x13 x13 3) (str! x13 x-st (at-st st-kk))
      (sub! x13 x-fp x-dsb) (lsr! x13 x13 3) (str! x13 x-st (at-st st-fp))
      (str! x-clo x-st (at-st st-clo))
      (sub! x13 x-dsp x-dsb) (lsr! x13 x13 3) (str! x13 x-st (at-st st-dsp))
      (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-rsb)) (sub! x13 x-rsp x14) (lsr! x13 x13 3) (str! x13 x-st (at-st st-rsp))
      (str! x-fuel x-st (at-st st-fuel))
      (movz! 0 (i64->int (fix why)))
      (ldp! 27 28 31 80) (ldp! 25 26 31 64) (ldp! 23 24 31 48) (ldp! 21 22 31 32) (ldp! 19 20 31 16) (ldp-post! 29 30 31 96)
      (ret!))))


(define resumed! (->* () unit)
  (lambda ()
    "Going on at the ip, a cell of `cur`'s: its code, if `cur` was compiled
     (its entry `r-count + s`, word `s`) and has code for that cell, else
     the cell interpreted (`NEXT`). Word `s`'s table of where to resume is
     at the offset that the table at `l-words` has for `s`: its length,
     times 8, then for each cell `k` its code's offset, or 0."
    (begin
      (bind! (get l-resume))
      ;; Entered so, register code has no link: it returns the stack's way.
      (mov! 30 31)
      (andl! x13 x-cur 3) (cmpi! x13 4) (bc! c-ne (get l-next))
      (add! x11 x-mem x-cur) (ldur! x10 x11 (- -4 (* 8 (i64->int f-entry))))
      (cmpi! x10 (* 8 (i64->int r-count))) (bc! c-lo (get l-next))
      (subi! x10 x10 (* 8 (i64->int r-count)))
      ;; Past the words compiled (a register word's entry is -1, C129):
      ;; given back, at the cell the ip is at.
      (adr! x16 (get l-words)) (ldr! x14 x16 0) (cmp! x10 x14) (bc! c-hs (get l-resume-give))
      (addi! x16 x16 8) (ldr-reg! x14 x16 x10)
      (adr! x16 (get l-start)) (add! x16 x16 x14)
      (subi! x15 x11 4) (sub! x15 x15 x-ip)
      (ldr! x14 x16 0)
      (let ((neg (label!)))
        (begin
          (cmpi! x15 0) (bc! c-lt neg)
          (cmp! x15 x14) (bc! c-hs (get l-next))
          (add! x16 x16 x15) (ldr! x14 x16 8) (cbz! x14 (get l-next))
          (adr! x16 (get l-start)) (add! x16 x16 x14) (br! x16)
          ;; Below 0, register code's point to resume at after a call
          ;; (C129): the table's second half; past it, a poll's, given back.
          (bind! neg)
          (sub! x15 31 x15) (cmp! x15 x14) (bc! c-hs (get l-resume-give))
          (add! x16 x16 x14) (add! x16 x16 x15) (ldr! x14 x16 8) (cbz! x14 (get l-resume-give))
          (adr! x16 (get l-start)) (add! x16 x16 x14) (br! x16))))))

"A prompt's and a mark's entries begin with these (machine.kfx's
 `prompt-mark`, `mark-mark`)."
(define prompt-mark-word i64 51)
(define mark-mark-word i64 43)

(define machine! (->* () unit)
  (lambda ()
    "The whole machine: its entry, `NEXT`, the ways out, the table, and a
     routine for each number."
    (let ((word (label!)) (table (label!)) (skip (label!)) (loop (label!)) (base (get hand-labels)))
      (begin
        (set hand-labels (+ base (i64->int r-count)))
        (set l-next (label!)) (set l-give (label!)) (set l-give-pre (label!)) (set l-ran-out (label!)) (set l-pop-return (label!))
        (set l-resume (label!)) (set l-resume-give (label!)) (set l-misaligned (label!))
        (bind! (get l-entry))
        (entry!)
        (resumed!)
        ;; NEXT: the cell, as tier 1's `run!` takes it: none if out of fuel
        ;; (tier 1 then polls or stops), else one step's fuel spent.
        (bind! (get l-next))
        (mov! x-cell x-ip)
        (cbz! x-fuel (get l-give-pre))
        (subi! x-fuel x-fuel 1)
        (ldr-post! x-w x-ip -8)
        (tstl! x-w 3)
        (bc! c-ne word)
        (cmpi! x-w (* 8 (i64->int r-count)))
        (give-if! c-hs)
        (lsr! x10 x-w 1)
        (adr! x16 table)
        (add! x16 x16 x10)
        (br! x16)
        (bind! word)
        (word-entered!)
        ;; Giving back: the step's fuel returned, if it was spent.
        (bind! (get l-give))
        (addi! x-fuel x-fuel 1)
        (bind! (get l-give-pre))
        (leave! gave-back)
        (bind! (get l-ran-out))
        (leave! ran-out)
        (bind! (get l-misaligned))
        (mov! x-cell x-ip) (leave! misaligned)
        (bind! (get l-resume-give))
        (mov! x-cell x-ip) (b! (get l-give-pre))
        ;; A return, as tier 1's `pop-return!`: a prompt's or a mark's entry
        ;; passed by.
        (bind! (get l-pop-return))
        (bind! loop)
        (ldr! x16 x-st (at-st st-rsb)) (cmp! x-rsp x16) (bc! c-ls (get l-ran-out))
        (ldur! x13 x-rsp -32)
        (cmpi! x13 (i64->int prompt-mark-word)) (bc! c-eq skip)
        (cmpi! x13 (i64->int mark-mark-word)) (bc! c-eq skip)
        (mov! x-cur x13)
        (ldur! x14 x-rsp -24) (ldur! x15 x-rsp -16) (ldur! x-clo x-rsp -8) (subi! x-rsp x-rsp 32)
        (add! x-ip x-mem x-cur) (subi! x-ip x-ip 4) (sub! x-ip x-ip x14)
        (add! x-fp x-dsb x15)
        (resume!)
        (bind! skip)
        (subi! x-rsp x-rsp 32) (b! loop)
        (bind! table)
        (table! 0 base)
        (routines! 0 base)))))

"Tier 4 (C128): each of the listing's words compiled, cell by cell, to
 its routine's code here, the dispatch between cells gone, the ip kept in
 step, so that code and cells mix: a call, a return or an entry goes to
 a cell's code if it has some (`resumed!`), else interprets it. As
 Fixpt's `assemble_word`, of its hand machine's routines (Fixpt's
 `native.fx` compiles for Fixpt's own machine, its stacks and registers,
 not this one's)."
(define hand-compiled (ref bool @c) (new #f))
(define words-compiled (ref int @c) (new 0))
"Longer words are not compiled: their branches' reach (a megabyte)."
(define compiled-cells-most i64 4000)

(define-rec
  (cells-in (->* (i64 i64) i64)
    (lambda (w k) "Word `w`'s cells from `k`: how many." (if (field-ok? w k) (cells-in w (i64+ k 1)) (i64- k f-cell0)))))

(define-rec
  (starts! (->* (i64 i64 i64 (flatarrayof i64 @c)) unit)
    (lambda (w i n at)
      "Which of `w`'s cells from `i` start one (a routine's operands do
       not): 1 in `at`, by cell."
      (if (i64>= i n)
          #u
          (let ((c (slot-of w (i64+ f-cell0 i))))
            (begin
              (flatarray-set-i64! at i 1)
              (starts! w (if (and (is-fixnum? c) (i64>= (fix-val c) 0) (i64< (fix-val c) r-count))
                             (i64+ i (i64+ 1 (operand-count (fix-val c))))
                             (i64+ i 1))
                       n at)))))))

(define-rec
  (next-start (->* ((flatarrayof i64 @c) i64 i64) i64)
    (lambda (at i n) (cond ((i64>= i n) n) ((i64= (flatarray-ref-i64 at i) 1) i) (else (next-start at (i64+ i 1) n))))))

(define-rec
  (cells-compiled! (->* (i64 i64 i64 (flatarrayof i64 @c) int) unit)
    (lambda (w i n at base)
      "Cell `i` on of word `w`, of `n`, each start's code at label `base +
       i`: `NEXT`'s step, then its routine with the next cell's code and a
       branch's target's for its `NEXT`; a word, entered."
      (if (i64>= i n)
          #u
          (if (not (i64= (flatarray-ref-i64 at i) 1))
              (cells-compiled! w (i64+ i 1) n at base)
              (let ((c (slot-of w (i64+ f-cell0 i))) (nx (next-start at (i64+ i 1) n)))
                (begin
                  (bind! (+ base (i64->int i)))
                  (mov! x-cell x-ip) (cbz! x-fuel (get l-give-pre)) (subi! x-fuel x-fuel 1) (ldr-post! x-w x-ip -8)
                  (set h-cont (+ base (i64->int nx)))
                  (set h-target -1)
                  (cond ((not (is-fixnum? c)) (word-entered!))
                        ((and (i64>= (fix-val c) 0) (i64< (fix-val c) r-count))
                         (begin
                           (if (or (i64= (fix-val c) r-branch) (i64= (fix-val c) r-zbranch))
                               (let ((t (i64+ i (i64+ 2 (fix-val (slot-of w (i64+ f-cell0 (i64+ i 1))))))))
                                 (if (and (i64>= t 0) (i64< t n) (i64= (flatarray-ref-i64 at t) 1))
                                     (set h-target (+ base (i64->int t)))
                                     #u))
                               #u)
                           (entered! (i64->int (fix-val c)))))
                        (else (b! (get l-give))))
                  (cells-compiled! w nx n at base))))))))

(define-rec
  (resume-table! (->* ((flatarrayof i64 @c) int i64 i64) unit)
    (lambda (at base n k)
      "A word's table of where to resume, from cell `k`: the offset of its
       code, if it starts one, else 0."
      (if (i64>= k (i64+ f-cell0 n))
          #u
          (begin
            (if (and (i64>= k f-cell0) (i64= (flatarray-ref-i64 at (i64- k f-cell0)) 1))
                (d! (offset-of (+ base (i64->int (i64- k f-cell0)))))
                (d! (ins 0)))
            (resume-table! at base n (i64+ k 1)))))))

(define-rec
  (zeros! (->* (i64) unit) (lambda (k) "`k` entries of 0." (if (i64<= k 0) #u (begin (d! (ins 0)) (zeros! (i64- k 1)))))))

(define word-compiled! (->* (i64 int int) unit)
  (lambda (w n-cells rt)
    "Word `w` compiled; `rt` the label of its table of where to resume."
    (let* ((n (int->i64 n-cells))
           (at (the (flatarrayof i64 @c) (make-flatarray-i64 (i64+ n 1) 0)))
           (base (get hand-labels))
           (give (+ base (+ n-cells 1))) (give-pre (+ base (+ n-cells 2)))
           (machine-give (get l-give)) (machine-give-pre (get l-give-pre)))
      (begin
          (set hand-labels (+ give-pre 1))
          (starts! w 0 n at)
          (set l-give give) (set l-give-pre give-pre)
          (cells-compiled! w 0 n at base)
          (bind! (+ base n-cells)) (b! (get l-next))
          ;; Its own ways to give back, near.
          (bind! give) (addi! x-fuel x-fuel 1)
          (bind! give-pre) (b! machine-give-pre)
          (set l-give machine-give) (set l-give-pre machine-give-pre)
          (set h-cont -1) (set h-target -1)
          (data-label! rt)
          (d! (ins (* 8 (i64->int (i64+ f-cell0 n)))))
          (resume-table! at base n 0)
          (zeros! (i64+ f-cell0 n))))))

"Tier 5 (C130): register words compiled, as Fixpt's
 `assemble_register_word` compiles them (`cellular/regcode.rs`), into
 this machine: `RESULT` in `x0`, `REGk` in `xk`, `REG0` `clo`. Each
 instruction counts its step and keeps its place in `x12`, as a cell, so
 that what it does not do it gives back to tier 1's register code
 (machine.kfx's `reg-op!`), the registers in the state. A call returns
 by the data stack, as stack code's do; the table of where to resume has
 a second half, the points after a call, which pop `RESULT` (`resumed!`)."
(define sub-const! (->* (int int int) unit)
  (lambda (d n k) (if (< k 4096) (subi! d n k) (begin (movz! x16 k) (sub! d n x16)))))
(define add-const! (->* (int int int) unit)
  (lambda (d n k) (if (< k 4096) (addi! d n k) (begin (movz! x16 k) (add! d n x16)))))
(define reg-of (->* (int) int) (lambda (k) (if (= k 0) x-clo k)))
(define opnd! (->* (int int) unit)
  (lambda (d j) "Operand `j` of the instruction at `x12`." (ldur! d x-cell (* -8 (+ j 1)))))
(define at-field (->* (i64) int) (lambda (f) (- -4 (* 8 (i64->int f)))))

(define op2-fast! (->* (i64 int) unit)
  (lambda (r y)
    "`RESULT` := cellular routine `r` of `RESULT` and `y`, on fixnums; past
     them, or of another routine, given back."
    (cond ((i64= r r-eq) (begin (cmp! 0 y) (boolean-of! c-eq) (mov! 0 x13)))
          ((or (i64= r r-int-add) (i64= r r-add) (i64= r r-int-sub) (i64= r r-sub))
           (begin
             (orr! x15 0 y) (tstl! x15 3) (give-if! c-ne)
             (if (or (i64= r r-int-add) (i64= r r-add)) (adds! x15 0 y) (subs! x15 0 y))
             (give-if! c-vs) (mov! 0 x15)))
          ((or (i64= r r-int-less) (i64= r r-less) (i64= r r-int-eq))
           (begin
             (orr! x15 0 y) (tstl! x15 3) (give-if! c-ne)
             (cmp! 0 y) (boolean-of! (if (i64= r r-int-eq) c-eq c-lt)) (mov! 0 x13)))
          (else (b! (get l-give))))))

(define-rec
  (fill-false! (->* (int) unit)
    (lambda (m) (if (<= m 0) #u (begin (str-post! x13 x-dsp 8) (fill-false! (- m 1)))))))

(define return-pushed! (->* (i64) unit)
  (lambda (nx)
    "A return entry to this word's point after a call, `-nx`: given back
     if there is no room for it."
    (begin
      (ldr! x16 x-st (at-st st-rs-end)) (cmp! x-rsp x16) (give-if! c-hs)
      (movz! x13 (* 8 (i64->int nx))) (sub! x13 31 x13) (sub! x14 x-fp x-dsb)
      (stp! x-cur x13 x-rsp 0) (stp! x14 x-clo x-rsp 16) (addi! x-rsp x-rsp 32))))

(define-rec
  (frees-stored! (->* (int int) unit)
    (lambda (r n) (if (> r n) #u (begin (stur! r x11 (- -24 (* 8 (- r 1)))) (frees-stored! (+ r 1) n))))))

"The frame's slot that keeps the link, past `save M`'s `M` (C131); -1
 before one, a leaf's link staying in `x30`."
(define h-link (ref int @c) (new -1))

(define link-reloaded! (->* (int) unit)
  (lambda (m) "`x30` the link again, after a call." (if (>= m 0) (ldr! 30 x-fp (* 8 m)) (mov! 30 31))))

(define entry-address! (->* (int int) unit)
  (lambda (r none)
    "`x16` the code of register word `r`'s first instruction past `args`,
     by the tables past the code's start; to `none` if it has none."
    (begin
      (ldr! x13 x-st (at-st st-start))
      (add! x14 x-mem r) (ldur! x15 x14 (at-field f-entry))
      (cmpi! x15 (* 8 (i64->int r-count))) (bc! c-lo none)
      (subi! x15 x15 (* 8 (i64->int r-count)))
      (ldr! x14 x13 8) (cmp! x15 x14) (bc! c-hs none)
      (add! x16 x13 x15) (ldr! x14 x16 16)
      (add! x16 x13 x14) (ldr! x14 x16 (* 8 (+ 1 (+ (i64->int f-cell0) 2))))
      (add! x16 x13 x14))))

(define-rec
  (args-pushed! (->* (int int) unit)
    (lambda (r n) (if (> r n) #u (begin (str-post! r x-dsp 8) (args-pushed! (+ r 1) n))))))

"Tier 6 (C138, C210), what both machines share: which register words it
 compiles (those that never allocate), their blocks, and the labels of
 their tier 6 code, its ways out and its ways in. Each machine emits its
 own code from these (hand-x64.kfx's `y6-…`, this file's `t6-…`)."
(define hand-direct (ref bool @c) (new #f))
"Where tier 6 was gone into: the link tier 5's code had then
 (hand-x64.kfx's; arm64 keeps it in the bottom record, C210)."
(define st-t6link int 33)
(define words-direct (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define l-materialize (ref int @c) (new 0))

(define direct-op? (->* (i64 i64 i64 i64 bool bool) bool)
  (lambda (op a b c allocs fuller)
    "Whether tier 6 has register operation `op`, of operands `a`, `b`, `c`;
     with `allocs`, the allocations tier 5 makes itself, at the heap's top,
     too (C147, C211): where tier 5 would give back to collect first, tier
     6 leaves, its records written as return entries, so the collector
     never sees one; with `fuller`, those arm64's tier 5 does itself since
     (C212): `%make-box`, `%make-frozen`, `setfield`, `%fx26-procedure?`
     and `%fx26-mul`."
    (cond ((i64= op ro-cellular) (and allocs (i64= a r-cons) (i64= b 2)))
          ((i64= op ro-prim)
           (or (and allocs (i64= (prim-op a) o-region-cons) (i64= b 3))
               (and fuller (or (and (i64= (prim-op a) o-make-box) (i64= b 1))
                               (and (i64= (prim-op a) o-make-frozen) (i64>= b 1) (i64<= b register-regs))))))
          ((i64= op ro-lambda) (and allocs (i64<= b register-regs) (i64= c r-closure)))
          ((i64= op ro-setfield) fuller)
          ((i64= op ro-prim1) (and fuller (i64= (prim-op a) o-procedure)))
          ((or (i64= op ro-prim2) (i64= op ro-prim2imm)) (and fuller (i64= (prim-op a) o-mul)))
          ((or (i64= op ro-op2) (i64= op ro-op2imm))
           (or (i64= a r-eq) (i64= a r-int-add) (i64= a r-add) (i64= a r-int-sub) (i64= a r-sub)
               (i64= a r-int-less) (i64= a r-less) (i64= a r-int-eq)))
          ((i64= op ro-op1) (or (i64= a r-car) (i64= a r-cdr) (i64= a r-pair-car) (i64= a r-pair-cdr)))
          (else
            (or (i64= op ro-args) (i64= op ro-const) (i64= op ro-global) (i64= op ro-setglbl) (i64= op ro-reg)
                (i64= op ro-setreg) (i64= op ro-movereg) (i64= op ro-lexical) (i64= op ro-save) (i64= op ro-pop)
                (i64= op ro-stack) (i64= op ro-load) (i64= op ro-setstk) (i64= op ro-store) (i64= op ro-field)
                (i64= op ro-invoke) (i64= op ro-tailinvoke) (i64= op ro-invokeself) (i64= op ro-return)
                (i64= op ro-branch) (i64= op ro-branchf) (i64= op ro-brancht) (i64= op ro-global-guard))))))

(define-rec
  (direct-able? (->* (i64 i64 i64 bool bool) bool)
    (lambda (rw i n allocs fuller)
      "Whether every instruction of `rw` from `i`, of `n` cells, is tier 6's
       (with `allocs` and `fuller`, `direct-op?`'s)."
      (if (i64>= i n)
          #t
          (let* ((kk (i64+ f-cell0 i)) (op (fix-val (slot-of rw kk)))
                 (ops (rop-operands op))
                 (a (if (i64>= ops 1) (fix-val (slot-of rw (i64+ kk 1))) (the i64 0)))
                 (b (if (i64>= ops 2) (fix-val (slot-of rw (i64+ kk 2))) (the i64 0)))
                 (c (if (i64>= ops 3) (fix-val (slot-of rw (i64+ kk 3))) (the i64 0))))
            (and (direct-op? op a b c allocs fuller) (direct-able? rw (i64+ i (i64+ 1 ops)) n allocs fuller)))))))

"Compiling a word for tier 6: whether, its instructions' labels, their
 ways out, its tier 5 code's labels, and its blocks."
(define h-6 (ref bool @c) (new #f))
(define h-6-base (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define h-6-exits (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define h-6-tier5 (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define h-6-adapter (ref int @c) (new -1))
"While a word with tier 6 code is compiled: each block's first's way in
 to it, and where in its block each instruction is."
(define h-6-on (ref bool @c) (new #f))
(define h-6-ins (ref int @c) (new 0))
(define h-6-at (ref (flatarrayof i64 @c) @c) (new (make-flatarray-i64 1 0)))
(define h-6-of (ref (flatarrayof i64 @c) @c) (new (make-flatarray-i64 1 0)))

(define branch-target (->* (i64 i64) i64)
  (lambda (rw i)
    "Where register instruction `i` of `rw` may branch to, or -1."
    (let* ((kk (i64+ f-cell0 i)) (op (fix-val (slot-of rw kk))))
      (cond ((or (i64= op ro-branch) (i64= op ro-branchf) (i64= op ro-brancht))
             (i64+ i (i64+ 2 (fix-val (slot-of rw (i64+ kk 1))))))
            ((i64= op ro-global-guard) (i64+ i (i64+ 4 (fix-val (slot-of rw (i64+ kk 3))))))
            (else -1)))))

(define-rec
  (t6-leaders! (->* (i64 i64 i64 (flatarrayof i64 @c)) unit)
    (lambda (rw i n lead)
      "Which instructions from `i` begin a block, 1 in `lead`: a branch's
       target, what follows a branch, a call or a return."
      (if (i64>= i n)
          #u
          (let* ((kk (i64+ f-cell0 i)) (op (fix-val (slot-of rw kk)))
                 (nx (i64+ i (i64+ 1 (rop-operands op))))
                 (t (branch-target rw i)))
            (begin
              (if (and (i64>= t 0) (i64<= t n)) (flatarray-set-i64! lead t 1) #u)
              (if (or (i64>= t 0) (i64= op ro-invoke) (i64= op ro-tailinvoke) (i64= op ro-invokeself) (i64= op ro-return))
                  (flatarray-set-i64! lead nx 1)
                  #u)
              (t6-leaders! rw nx n lead)))))))

(define-rec
  (t6-blocks! (->* (i64 i64 i64 (flatarrayof i64 @c) i64 (flatarrayof i64 @c) (flatarrayof i64 @c) (flatarrayof i64 @c)) unit)
    (lambda (rw i n lead l at of len)
      "For each instruction from `i`, the block it is in begun at `l`: its
       place in it in `at`, the block's first in `of`; each block's length
       in `len`, by its first."
      (if (i64>= i n)
          #u
          (let* ((nx (i64+ i (i64+ 1 (rop-operands (fix-val (slot-of rw (i64+ f-cell0 i)))))))
                 (b (if (i64= (flatarray-ref-i64 lead i) 1) i l)))
            (begin
              (flatarray-set-i64! at i (flatarray-ref-i64 len b))
              (flatarray-set-i64! of i b)
              (flatarray-set-i64! len b (i64+ (flatarray-ref-i64 len b) 1))
              (t6-blocks! rw nx n lead b at of len)))))))

"A block's fuel, spent at its start: given back by its first's way out
 if there is not as much."
(define h-6-lead (ref (flatarrayof i64 @c) @c) (new (make-flatarray-i64 1 0)))
(define h-6-len (ref (flatarrayof i64 @c) @c) (new (make-flatarray-i64 1 0)))

(define t6-to (->* (int i64) int)
  (lambda (base t)
    "The label instruction `t` is branched to at, its code's at `base`:
     for tier 5's code of a word with tier 6 code, a block's first's way
     in to tier 6, so that a loop left goes back in."
    (if (and (not (get h-6)) (get h-6-on) (i64= (flatarray-ref-i64 (get h-6-lead) t) 1))
        (+ (get h-6-ins) (i64->int t))
        (+ base (i64->int t)))))

(define t6-prepared! (->* (i64 i64) unit)
  (lambda (rw n)
    "Register word `rw`'s tier 6 labels and blocks, before its tier 5
     code, whose branches and tables go to them."
    (let ((lead (the (flatarrayof i64 @c) (make-flatarray-i64 (i64+ n 1) 0)))
          (at (the (flatarrayof i64 @c) (make-flatarray-i64 (i64+ n 1) 0)))
          (of (the (flatarrayof i64 @c) (make-flatarray-i64 (i64+ n 1) 0)))
          (len (the (flatarrayof i64 @c) (make-flatarray-i64 (i64+ n 1) 0)))
          (n-cells (i64->int n)))
      (begin
        (set h-6-base (get hand-labels)) (set hand-labels (+ (get hand-labels) (+ n-cells 1)))
        (set h-6-exits (get hand-labels)) (set hand-labels (+ (get hand-labels) (+ n-cells 1)))
        (set h-6-ins (get hand-labels)) (set hand-labels (+ (get hand-labels) (+ n-cells 1)))
        (flatarray-set-i64! lead 2 1) (t6-leaders! rw 0 n lead)
        (t6-blocks! rw 2 n lead 2 at of len)
        (set h-6-lead lead) (set h-6-at at) (set h-6-of of) (set h-6-len len)
        (set h-6-adapter (+ (get h-6-ins) 2))
        (set h-6-on #t)))))

"Tier 6 on arm64 (C210), as hand-x64.kfx's (C138) but for what arm64
 changes: a call is a `bl` (or `blr`), the callee's link in `x30`, which
 the caller keeps in its record, `(x30 nx fp clo cur link)` from the
 machine stack's top, 48 bytes (`sp` kept 16-aligned), and takes back
 after; so a return is a `ret`, which the processor predicts. `link` is
 tier 5's: where tier 5's code of the same call returns to, which the
 callee's `save` keeps in its frame as tier 5's would, so that once tier 6
 is left its frames return by their links, not the stack's way. The
 bottom record is `(1 1 - - - link)`, the link tier 5's code had where it
 went in. The registers are tier 5's, all in machine registers already,
 so a way in or out moves none. An instruction's place in `x12` is made
 only by those that read an operand there."
"By instruction, the label of tier 5's code just past its call, where
 its callee returns to by its link (C210)."
(define h-6-after (ref (flatarrayof i64 @c) @c) (new (make-flatarray-i64 1 0)))
(define after-call! (->* (i64) unit)
  (lambda (i)
    "Tier 5's point past instruction `i`'s call, labelled for tier 6."
    (if (get h-6-on)
        (let ((l (label!))) (begin (bind! l) (flatarray-set-i64! (get h-6-after) i (int->i64 l))))
        #u)))
(define subsi! (->* (int int int) unit) (lambda (d n i) (e! ((with a64 arm-subs-imm) d n i))))

(define reads-operands? (->* (i64) bool)
  (lambda (op)
    "Whether register operation `op` reads an operand from the word, at
     its place in `x12`."
    (or (i64= op ro-const) (i64= op ro-global) (i64= op ro-setglbl) (i64= op ro-op2imm) (i64= op ro-global-guard)
        (i64= op ro-lambda) (i64= op ro-prim2imm))))

(define t6-called! (->* (int int int i64 int) unit)
  (lambda (l r new-cur nx after)
    "A call of tier 6 code at label `l`, or if it is -1 at the address in
     `r`, `cur` then `new-cur` (a register, or -1 for this one), the
     closure in `x0` (none for `invokeself`): the caller's record pushed,
     with tier 5's point past the same call, `after`; its place on the
     return stack kept; and after it, popped."
    (begin
      (limits!) (ldr! x16 x-st (at-st st-rs-end)) (cmp! x-rsp x16) (give-if! c-hs)
      (movz! x13 (* 8 (i64->int (i64+ f-cell0 nx)))) (sub! x13 31 x13)
      (stp-pre! 30 x13 31 -48) (stp! x-fp x-clo 31 16) (adr! x16 after) (stp! x-cur x16 31 32)
      (addi! x-rsp x-rsp 32)
      (if (< new-cur 0) #u (begin (mov! x-clo 0) (mov! x-cur new-cur)))
      (if (< l 0) (blr! r) (bl! l))
      (ldp! x-fp x-clo 31 16) (ldr! x-cur 31 32) (ldp-post! 30 x13 31 48)
      (subi! x-rsp x-rsp 32))))

(define t6-invoked! (->* (bool int i64 int) unit)
  (lambda (tail n nx after)
    "`invoke n` (or `tailinvoke`) of the closure in `x0`, if its word's
     twin has tier 6 code of `n` arguments; else out, to tier 5."
    (begin
      (closure-in! 0)
      (ldur! x13 x11 (at-field f-word)) (add! x14 x-mem x13)
      (ldur! x10 x14 (at-field f-twin)) (cmpi! x10 3) (give-if! c-eq)
      (add! x14 x-mem x10) (ldur! x15 x14 (at-field (i64+ f-cell0 1))) (cmpi! x15 (* 8 n)) (give-if! c-ne)
      ;; Its tier 6 code: field 1 of its table, by the tables past the
      ;; code's start.
      (ldur! x15 x14 (at-field f-entry))
      (cmpi! x15 (* 8 (i64->int r-count))) (give-if! c-lo)
      (subi! x15 x15 (* 8 (i64->int r-count)))
      (ldr! x13 x-st (at-st st-start)) (ldr! x16 x13 8) (cmp! x15 x16) (give-if! c-hs)
      (add! x16 x13 x15) (ldr! x16 x16 16)
      (add! x16 x13 x16) (ldr! x17 x16 16) (cbz! x17 (get l-give))
      (add! x17 x13 x17)
      (if tail
          (begin (limits!) (mov! x-clo 0) (mov! x-cur x10) (br! x17))
          (t6-called! -1 x17 x10 nx after)))))

(define t6-returned! (->* () unit)
  (lambda ()
    "`return`: to the caller's code; over the bottom record, out, to tier
     5's, which returns to tier 5's caller."
    (begin (ldr! x13 31 8) (cmpi! x13 1) (give-if! c-eq) (ret!))))

(define-rec
  (t6-exits! (->* (i64 i64 (flatarrayof i64 @c) (flatarrayof i64 @c) (flatarrayof i64 @c) (flatarrayof i64 @c)) unit)
    (lambda (i n starts at of len)
      "Each instruction's way out: the fuel of its block not spent given
       back (it, and those after it), the records written, on in tier 5
       at it."
      (if (i64>= i n)
          #u
          (begin
            (if (and (i64>= i 2) (i64= (flatarray-ref-i64 starts i) 1))
                (let ((back (i64- (flatarray-ref-i64 len (flatarray-ref-i64 of i)) (flatarray-ref-i64 at i))))
                  (begin
                    (bind! (+ (get h-6-exits) (i64->int i)))
                    (if (i64> back 0) (addi! x-fuel x-fuel (i64->int back)) #u)
                    (adr! x16 (+ (get h-6-tier5) (i64->int i)))
                    (b! (get l-materialize))))
                #u)
            (t6-exits! (i64+ i 1) n starts at of len))))))

(define materialize! (->* (int) unit)
  (lambda (l)
    "Tier 6 left, for tier 5's code at `x16`: each record, from the
     innermost, written in the place it kept on the return stack, as the
     entry it stands for; all popped, the bottom record too; the link the
     innermost's, tier 5's, from the record on top."
    (let ((loop (label!)) (done (label!)))
      (begin
        (bind! l)
        (addi! x11 31 0) (mov! x14 x-rsp)
        (bind! loop)
        (ldr! x13 x11 8) (cmpi! x13 1) (bc! c-eq done)
        (subi! x14 x14 32)
        (ldr! x13 x11 32) (str! x13 x14 0)
        (ldr! x13 x11 8) (str! x13 x14 8)
        (ldr! x13 x11 16) (sub! x13 x13 x-dsb) (str! x13 x14 16)
        (ldr! x13 x11 24) (str! x13 x14 24)
        (addi! x11 x11 48) (b! loop)
        (bind! done)
        (ldr! 30 31 40) (addi! 31 x11 48)
        (br! x16)))))

(define-rec
  (frozen-fields! (->* (int int) unit)
    (lambda (r n)
      "`REGr`… to `REG(n+1)` as a frozen bloblet's fields at `x16`, its
       header: `REG2` just below the trailer, the last just above the
       header."
      (if (> r (+ n 1)) #u (begin (str! r x16 (* 8 (- (+ n 2) r))) (frozen-fields! (+ r 1) n))))))

(define reg-body! (->* (i64 i64 i64 int (flatarrayof i64 @c)) unit)
  (lambda (rw i n base resumes)
    "What register instruction `i` of `rw`'s `n` cells does, its
     instructions at labels from `base`, for tier 5, or for tier 6 if
     `h-6`; for tier 5, a point after a call marked in `resumes`."
    (let* ((kk (i64+ f-cell0 i))
           (op (fix-val (slot-of rw kk)))
           (o (lambda ((j int)) (fix-val (slot-of rw (i64+ kk (int->i64 (+ j 1)))))))
           (nx (i64+ i (i64+ 1 (rop-operands op))))
           (to (lambda ((ops int) (off i64)) (t6-to base (i64+ i (i64+ (int->i64 (+ ops 1)) off))))))
      (begin
        (cond
          ((or (i64= op ro-args) (i64= op ro-vargs)) #u)
          ((i64= op ro-const) (opnd! 0 0))
          ((i64= op ro-global) (begin (opnd! x16 0) (add! x16 x-mem x16) (ldur! 0 x16 (at-field f-value))))
          ((i64= op ro-setglbl)
           (begin
             (opnd! x16 0) (add! x16 x-mem x16) (stur! 0 x16 (at-field f-value))
             (ldur! x13 x16 (at-field f-writes)) (addi! x13 x13 8) (stur! x13 x16 (at-field f-writes))))
          ((i64= op ro-reg) (mov! 0 (reg-of (i64->int (o 0)))))
          ((i64= op ro-setreg) (mov! (reg-of (i64->int (o 0))) 0))
          ((i64= op ro-movereg) (mov! (reg-of (i64->int (o 1))) (reg-of (i64->int (o 0)))))
          ((i64= op ro-lexical)
           (begin
             (andl! x14 x-clo 3) (cmpi! x14 4) (give-if! c-ne) (add! x11 x-mem x-clo)
             (movz! x13 (* 8 (i64->int (i64+ f-free0 (o 0))))) (field-read!) (mov! 0 x16)))
          ((i64= op ro-save)
           (let ((m (i64->int (o 0))))
             (begin
               (add-const! x16 x-dsp (* 8 (+ m 1)))
               (ldr! x13 x-st (at-st st-ds-lim)) (cmp! x16 x13) (give-if! c-hi)
               (ldr! x13 x-st (at-st st-ds-end)) (cmp! x16 x13) (give-if! c-hi)
               (ldr! x13 x-st (at-st st-rs-lim)) (cmp! x-rsp x13) (give-if! c-hs)
               (mov! x-fp x-dsp) (movz! x13 3)
               (if (<= m 16)
                   (fill-false! m)
                   (let ((loop (label!)))
                     (begin (sub-const! x15 x16 8) (bind! loop) (str-post! x13 x-dsp 8) (cmp! x-dsp x15) (bc! c-lo loop))))
               ;; The link (C131): 8-aligned, a fixnum to the collector;
               ;; tier 6's, tier 5's, from its caller's record (C210).
               (if (get h-6) (begin (ldr! x13 31 40) (str-post! x13 x-dsp 8)) (str-post! 30 x-dsp 8))
               (set h-link m))))
          ((i64= op ro-pop)
           (begin (sub-const! x16 x-dsp (* 8 (+ (i64->int (o 0)) 1))) (cmp! x16 x-dsb) (give-if! c-lo) (mov! x-dsp x16)))
          ((or (i64= op ro-stack) (i64= op ro-load) (i64= op ro-setstk) (i64= op ro-store))
           (let ((slot (i64->int (if (or (i64= op ro-stack) (i64= op ro-setstk)) (o 0) (o 1))))
                 (r (if (or (i64= op ro-stack) (i64= op ro-setstk)) 0 (reg-of (i64->int (o 0))))))
             (begin
               (add-const! x14 x-fp (* 8 slot)) (cmp! x14 x-dsp) (give-if! c-hs)
               (if (or (i64= op ro-stack) (i64= op ro-load)) (ldr! r x14 0) (str! r x14 0)))))
          ((i64= op ro-op1)
           (let ((r (o 0)))
             (if (or (i64= r r-car) (i64= r r-cdr) (i64= r r-pair-car) (i64= r r-pair-cdr))
                 (begin
                   (andl! x14 0 3) (cmpi! x14 1) (give-if! c-ne) (add! x15 x-mem 0)
                   (ldur! 0 x15 (if (or (i64= r r-car) (i64= r r-pair-car)) -1 7)))
                 (b! (get l-give)))))
          ((i64= op ro-op2) (op2-fast! (o 0) (reg-of (i64->int (o 1)))))
          ((i64= op ro-op2imm) (begin (opnd! x14 1) (op2-fast! (o 0) x14)))
          ((i64= op ro-field)
           (begin
             (andl! x14 0 3) (cmpi! x14 4) (give-if! c-ne) (add! x11 x-mem 0)
             (movz! x13 (* 8 (i64->int (o 0)))) (field-read!) (mov! 0 x16)))
          ((and (i64= op ro-cellular) (i64= (o 0) r-cons) (i64= (o 1) 2))
           (begin
             (allocating! 2 31) (stp! 1 2 x16 0)
             (addi! x15 x13 2) (str! x15 x-st (at-st st-top)) (sub! 0 x16 x-mem) (addi! 0 0 1)))
          ((and (i64= op ro-prim) (i64= (prim-op (o 0)) o-region-cons) (i64= (o 1) 3))
           (begin
             (allocating! 2 31) (stp! 2 3 x16 0)
             (addi! x15 x13 2) (str! x15 x-st (at-st st-top)) (sub! 0 x16 x-mem) (addi! 0 0 1)))
          ((and (i64= op ro-lambda) (i64<= (o 1) register-regs) (i64= (o 2) r-closure))
           (let ((n (i64->int (o 1))))
             (begin
               ;; As `closed!` lays a closure out, its values from the registers.
               (opnd! x10 0) (movz! x17 (* 8 n))
               (allocating! 3 x17)
               (movz! x15 (+ 6 (* 8 (i64->int k-closure)))) (movz! x14 (+ n 2)) (lsl! x14 x14 14) (orr! x15 x15 x14)
               (str! x15 x16 0)
               (add-const! x11 x16 (+ (* 8 n) 24))
               (movz! x14 (+ (* 8 n) 21)) (stur! x14 x11 -8)
               (stur! x10 x11 -16)
               (frees-stored! 1 n)
               (addi! x14 x13 (+ 3 n)) (str! x14 x-st (at-st st-top))
               (sub! x14 x11 x-mem) (addi! 0 x14 4))))
          ((and (i64= op ro-prim) (i64= (prim-op (o 0)) o-make-box) (i64= (o 1) 1))
           (begin
             ;; As tier 1's `make-bloblet!`: its header, `REG1`, its trailer.
             (allocating! 3 31)
             (movz! x15 (+ (+ 6 (* 8 (i64->int k-box))) (* 2 16384))) (str! x15 x16 0)
             (str! 1 x16 8) (movz! x14 21) (str! x14 x16 16)
             (addi! x15 x13 3) (str! x15 x-st (at-st st-top))
             (sub! 0 x16 x-mem) (addi! 0 0 28)))
          ((and (i64= op ro-prim) (i64= (prim-op (o 0)) o-make-frozen) (i64>= (o 1) 1) (i64<= (o 1) register-regs))
           (let ((n (- (i64->int (o 1)) 1)) (kind (label!)))
             (begin
               ;; `REG1` the kind, a sum's or a product's, else given back;
               ;; `REG2`… the fields, from the header up the last first;
               ;; frozen whole, as tier 1's `frozen-of!`.
               (movz! x14 (* 8 (i64->int k-sum))) (cmp! 1 x14) (bc! c-eq kind)
               (movz! x14 (* 8 (i64->int k-product))) (cmp! 1 x14) (give-if! c-ne)
               (bind! kind)
               (allocating! (+ n 2) 31)
               (movz! x15 (+ 6 12288)) (movz! x14 (+ n 1)) (lsl! x14 x14 14) (orr! x15 x15 x14) (add! x15 x15 1)
               (str! x15 x16 0)
               (frozen-fields! 2 n)
               (movz! x14 (+ (* 8 n) 13)) (str! x14 x16 (* 8 (+ n 1)))
               (addi! x15 x13 (+ n 2)) (str! x15 x-st (at-st st-top))
               (sub! 0 x16 x-mem) (addi! 0 0 (+ (* 8 (+ n 2)) 4)))))
          ((i64= op ro-setfield)
           (begin
             ;; Where tier 1's `field-ok?` allows, as a field is read; no
             ;; barrier, as tier 1's `slot-set!`.
             (andl! x14 0 3) (cmpi! x14 4) (give-if! c-ne) (add! x11 x-mem 0)
             (movz! x13 (* 8 (i64->int (o 0)))) (fields-of! 0)
             (cmp! x13 x14) (give-if! c-lt) (cmp! x13 x15) (give-if! c-hi)
             (sub! x16 x11 x13) (stur! (reg-of (i64->int (o 1))) x16 -4)))
          ((and (i64= op ro-prim1) (i64= (prim-op (o 0)) o-procedure))
           (let ((header (label!)) (yes (label!)) (done (label!)))
             (begin
               ;; As tier 1's: a bloblet of one of six kinds.
               (movz! x13 3)
               (andl! x14 0 3) (cmpi! x14 4) (bc! c-ne done)
               (add! x11 x-mem 0) (ldur! x15 x11 -12) (andl! x14 x15 3) (cmpi! x14 5) (bc! c-ne header)
               (sub! x14 x11 x15) (ldur! x15 x14 -7)
               (bind! header)
               (ubfx! x14 x15 3 8)
               (cmpi! x14 8) (bc! c-eq yes) (cmpi! x14 19) (bc! c-eq yes) (cmpi! x14 14) (bc! c-eq yes)
               (cmpi! x14 (i64->int k-closure)) (bc! c-eq yes) (cmpi! x14 (i64->int k-native-closure)) (bc! c-eq yes)
               (cmpi! x14 (i64->int k-continuation)) (bc! c-ne done)
               (bind! yes) (movz! x13 11)
               (bind! done) (mov! 0 x13))))
          ((and (or (i64= op ro-prim2) (i64= op ro-prim2imm)) (i64= (prim-op (o 0)) o-mul))
           (let ((y (if (i64= op ro-prim2) (reg-of (i64->int (o 1))) x14)))
             (begin
               ;; Of two fixnums, a fixnum, else given back (a bignum's).
               (if (i64= op ro-prim2imm) (opnd! x14 1) #u)
               (orr! x15 0 y) (tstl! x15 3) (give-if! c-ne)
               (asr! x15 0 3) (mul! x16 x15 y) (smulh! x17 x15 y) (asr! x15 x16 63) (cmp! x17 x15) (give-if! c-ne)
               (mov! 0 x16))))
          ((and (get h-6) (or (i64= op ro-invoke) (i64= op ro-tailinvoke)))
           (t6-invoked! (i64= op ro-tailinvoke) (i64->int (o 0)) nx (i64->int (flatarray-ref-i64 (get h-6-after) i))))
          ((and (get h-6) (i64= op ro-invokeself)) (t6-called! (+ base 2) -1 -1 nx (i64->int (flatarray-ref-i64 (get h-6-after) i))))
          ((and (get h-6) (i64= op ro-return)) (t6-returned!))
          ((or (i64= op ro-invoke) (i64= op ro-tailinvoke))
           (let ((tail (i64= op ro-tailinvoke)) (stack-code (label!)) (stack-way (label!)) (n (i64->int (o 0))))
             (begin
               (closure-in! 0)
               (ldur! x13 x11 (at-field f-word)) (add! x14 x-mem x13)
               (ldur! x10 x14 (at-field f-twin)) (cmpi! x10 3) (bc! c-eq stack-code)
               (add! x14 x-mem x10) (ldur! x15 x14 (at-field (i64+ f-cell0 1)))
               (cmpi! x15 (* 8 n)) (give-if! c-ne)
               (limits!)
               (if tail #u (return-pushed! (i64+ f-cell0 nx)))
               (mov! x-clo 0) (mov! x-cur x10)
               ;; Register code compiled: by `blr` (in tail position, `br`,
               ;; the link this one's), its value in `x0`.
               (entry-address! x10 stack-way)
               (if tail
                   (br! x16)
                   (begin (align-odd!) (blr! x16) (after-call! i) (link-reloaded! (get h-link)) (b! (+ base (i64->int nx)))))
               (bind! stack-way)
               (add! x-ip x-mem x-cur) (subi! x-ip x-ip (+ 4 (* 8 (+ (i64->int f-cell0) 2))))
               (resume!)
               ;; Stack code: the arguments its frame, as tier 1's `call!`.
               (bind! stack-code)
               (if (> n 8)
                   (b! (get l-give))
                   (begin
                     (mov! x10 x13)
                     (limits!)
                     (add-const! x16 x-dsp (* 8 n)) (ldr! x14 x-st (at-st st-ds-end)) (cmp! x16 x14) (give-if! c-hi)
                     (if tail #u (return-pushed! (i64+ f-cell0 nx)))
                     (mov! x-fp x-dsp) (args-pushed! 1 n)
                     (mov! x-clo 0) (mov! x-cur x10)
                     (add! x-ip x-mem x-cur) (subi! x-ip x-ip (+ 4 (* 8 (i64->int f-cell0))))
                     (resume!))))))
          ((i64= op ro-invokeself)
           (begin
             (limits!) (return-pushed! (i64+ f-cell0 nx))
             (align-odd!) (bl! (t6-to base 2)) (after-call! i) (link-reloaded! (get h-link))))
          ((i64= op ro-return)
           (let ((stack-way (label!)))
             (begin
               (ldr! x16 x-st (at-st st-rsb)) (cmp! x-rsp x16) (give-if! c-eq)
               ;; With a link, to the caller's code, the entry it pushed
               ;; popped (C131); else the stack's way.
               (cbz! 30 stack-way)
               (ldur! x13 x-rsp -32)
               (cmpi! x13 (i64->int prompt-mark-word)) (bc! c-eq stack-way)
               (cmpi! x13 (i64->int mark-mark-word)) (bc! c-eq stack-way)
               (mov! x-cur x13) (ldur! x14 x-rsp -16) (ldur! x-clo x-rsp -8) (subi! x-rsp x-rsp 32)
               (add! x-fp x-dsb x14) (br! 30)
               (bind! stack-way)
               (h-room!) (str-post! 0 x-dsp 8) (b! (get l-pop-return)))))
          ((i64= op ro-branch) (b! (to 1 (o 0))))
          ((i64= op ro-branchf) (begin (cmpi! 0 3) (bc! c-eq (to 1 (o 0)))))
          ((i64= op ro-brancht) (begin (cmpi! 0 3) (bc! c-ne (to 1 (o 0)))))
          ((i64= op ro-global-guard)
           (begin
             (opnd! x16 0) (add! x16 x-mem x16) (ldur! x13 x16 (at-field f-writes))
             (opnd! x14 1) (cmp! x13 x14) (bc! c-ne (to 3 (fix-val (slot-of rw (i64+ kk 3)))))))
          (else (b! (get l-give))))
        ;; Where a call or a call-out comes back to: its value on the data
        ;; stack, whether it ran here or was given back.
        (if (and (not (get h-6)) (or (i64= op ro-prim) (i64= op ro-lambda) (i64= op ro-cellular) (i64= op ro-invoke) (i64= op ro-invokeself)))
            (flatarray-set-i64! resumes nx (int->i64 (+ (get h-link) 2)))
            #u)))))

(define reg-ins! (->* (i64 i64 i64 int (flatarrayof i64 @c)) unit)
  (lambda (rw i n base resumes)
    "Register instruction `i` of `rw`'s `n` cells for tier 5, at label
     `base + i`, its place in `x12` and its step counted."
    (begin
      (bind! (+ base (i64->int i)))
      (add! x-cell x-mem x-cur) (sub-const! x-cell x-cell (+ 4 (* 8 (i64->int (i64+ f-cell0 i)))))
      (cbz! x-fuel (get l-give-pre)) (subi! x-fuel x-fuel 1)
      (reg-body! rw i n base resumes))))

(define t6-ins! (->* (i64 i64 i64 (flatarrayof i64 @c)) unit)
  (lambda (rw i n none)
    "Register instruction `i` of `rw`'s `n` cells for tier 6: at a block's
     first, the block's steps counted; its place in `x12` only if it reads
     an operand; its way out its own."
    (let ((kk (i64+ f-cell0 i)))
      (begin
        (bind! (+ (get h-6-base) (i64->int i)))
        (set l-give (+ (get h-6-exits) (i64->int i))) (set l-give-pre (get l-give))
        (if (i64= (flatarray-ref-i64 (get h-6-lead) i) 1)
            (begin (subsi! x-fuel x-fuel (i64->int (flatarray-ref-i64 (get h-6-len) i))) (bc! c-lo (get l-give)))
            #u)
        (if (reads-operands? (fix-val (slot-of rw kk)))
            (begin (add! x-cell x-mem x-cur) (sub-const! x-cell x-cell (+ 4 (* 8 (i64->int kk)))))
            #u)
        (reg-body! rw i n (get h-6-base) none)))))

(define-rec
  (t6-instructions! (->* (i64 i64 i64 (flatarrayof i64 @c)) unit)
    (lambda (rw i n none)
      (if (i64>= i n)
          #u
          (begin
            (t6-ins! rw i n none)
            (t6-instructions! rw (i64+ i (i64+ 1 (rop-operands (fix-val (slot-of rw (i64+ f-cell0 i)))))) n none))))))

(define-rec
  (t6-ways-in! (->* (i64 i64) unit)
    (lambda (i n)
      "For each block's first from `i`, its way in to tier 6 from tier 5,
       or from the tables: the bottom record pushed, with the link tier
       5's code had; on at it."
      (if (i64> i n)
          #u
          (begin
            (if (and (i64>= i 2) (i64< i n) (i64= (flatarray-ref-i64 (get h-6-lead) i) 1))
                (begin
                  (bind! (+ (get h-6-ins) (i64->int i)))
                  (movz! x13 1) (stp-pre! x13 x13 31 -48) (str! 30 31 40)
                  (b! (+ (get h-6-base) (i64->int i))))
                #u)
            (t6-ways-in! (i64+ i 1) n))))))

(define t6-compiled! (->* (i64 i64 int (flatarrayof i64 @c)) unit)
  (lambda (rw n base starts)
    "Register word `rw`'s tier 6 code, its tier 5 code at labels from
     `base`, and its ways in."
    (let ((n-cells (i64->int n)))
      (begin
        (set h-6-tier5 base)
        (set h-6 #t)
        (t6-instructions! rw 2 n (get h-6-lead))
        (set h-6 #f)
        ;; Past the last, as tier 5's.
        (bind! (+ (get h-6-base) n-cells)) (adr! x16 (+ base n-cells)) (b! (get l-materialize))
        (t6-exits! 0 n starts (get h-6-at) (get h-6-of) (get h-6-len))
        (t6-ways-in! 2 n)))))

(define-rec
  (reg-instructions! (->* (i64 i64 i64 int (flatarrayof i64 @c) (flatarrayof i64 @c)) unit)
    (lambda (rw i n base starts resumes)
      (if (i64>= i n)
          #u
          (let ((nx (i64+ i (i64+ 1 (rop-operands (fix-val (slot-of rw (i64+ f-cell0 i))))))))
            (begin
              (flatarray-set-i64! starts i 1)
              (reg-ins! rw i n base resumes)
              (reg-instructions! rw nx n base starts resumes)))))))

(define-rec
  (resumes-emitted! (->* (i64 i64 int int int (flatarrayof i64 @c)) unit)
    (lambda (i n base rbase rgive resumes)
      "For each point after a call: `RESULT` popped, and on."
      (if (i64>= i n)
          #u
          (begin
            (if (i64>= (flatarray-ref-i64 resumes i) 1)
                (begin
                  (bind! (+ rbase (i64->int i)))
                  (cmp! x-dsp x-dsb) (bc! c-ls rgive) (regs-zeroed! 1) (subi! x-dsp x-dsp 8) (ldr! 0 x-dsp 0)
                  (link-reloaded! (- (i64->int (flatarray-ref-i64 resumes i)) 2))
                  (b! (+ base (i64->int i))))
                #u)
            (resumes-emitted! (i64+ i 1) n base rbase rgive resumes))))))

(define-rec
  (reg-table! (->* (i64 i64 int int (flatarrayof i64 @c) bool) unit)
    (lambda (k n base rgive marks six)
      "A half of a register word's table: from field `k`, the code of each
       instruction `marks` marks, else the way to give back; if `six`, a
       block's first's way in to tier 6, so that a call (`entry-address!`
       reads instruction 2's) or a return goes into tier 6."
      (if (i64>= k (i64+ f-cell0 n))
          #u
          (begin
            (if (and (i64>= k f-cell0) (i64>= (flatarray-ref-i64 marks (i64- k f-cell0)) 1))
                (d! (offset-of (if (and six (i64= (flatarray-ref-i64 (get h-6-lead) (i64- k f-cell0)) 1))
                                   (+ (get h-6-ins) (i64->int (i64- k f-cell0)))
                                   (+ base (i64->int (i64- k f-cell0))))))
                (d! (offset-of rgive)))
            (reg-table! (i64+ k 1) n base rgive marks six))))))

(define register-compiled! (->* (i64 int int) unit)
  (lambda (rw n-cells rt)
    "Register word `rw` compiled; `rt` the label of its table, whose field
     1 is its tier 6 code, or 0 for none."
    (let* ((n (int->i64 n-cells))
           (starts (the (flatarrayof i64 @c) (make-flatarray-i64 (i64+ n 1) 0)))
           (resumes (the (flatarrayof i64 @c) (make-flatarray-i64 (i64+ n 1) 0)))
           (base (get hand-labels)) (rbase (+ base (+ n-cells 1)))
           (give (+ rbase (+ n-cells 1))) (give-pre (+ give 1)) (rgive (+ give 2))
           (machine-give (get l-give)) (machine-give-pre (get l-give-pre))
           (direct (and (get hand-direct) (direct-able? rw 0 n #t #t))))
      (begin
        (set hand-labels (+ rgive 1))
        (if direct (set words-direct (+ (get words-direct) 1)) #u)
        (set h-link -1)
        (set l-give give) (set l-give-pre give-pre)
        (if direct (begin (t6-prepared! rw n) (set h-6-after (make-flatarray-i64 (i64+ n 1) 0))) #u)
        (reg-instructions! rw 0 n base starts resumes)
        (bind! (+ base n-cells)) (b! give)
        (resumes-emitted! 0 n base rbase rgive resumes)
        (bind! give) (addi! x-fuel x-fuel 1)
        (bind! give-pre) (b! machine-give-pre)
        (bind! rgive) (b! (get l-resume-give))
        (if direct (t6-compiled! rw n base starts) #u)
        (set l-give machine-give) (set l-give-pre machine-give-pre)
        (data-label! rt)
        (d! (ins (* 8 (i64->int (i64+ f-cell0 n)))))
        (d! (offset-of rgive)) (d! (if direct (offset-of (+ (get h-6-base) 2)) (ins 0)))
        (reg-table! 2 n base rgive starts direct)
        (reg-table! 0 n rbase rgive resumes #f)
        (set h-6-adapter -1) (set h-6-on #f)))))

(define-rec
  (registers-compiled! (->* ((listof named @c) int (listof int @c)) (listof int @c))
    (lambda (rs s rts)
      "Each register word that is its word's twin, compiled, word `s` on;
       its entry made `r-count + s`. Their tables' labels, the last first."
      (if (null? rs)
          rts
          (let ((rw (named-value (car rs))))
            (if (and (i64= (slot-of (slot-of rw f-twin) f-twin) rw)
                     (i64<= (cells-in rw f-cell0) compiled-cells-most))
                (let ((rt (label!)))
                  (begin
                    (register-compiled! rw (i64->int (cells-in rw f-cell0)) rt)
                    (slot-set! rw f-entry (fix (i64+ r-count (int->i64 s))))
                    (registers-compiled! (cdr rs) (+ s 1) (cons rt rts))))
                (registers-compiled! (cdr rs) s rts)))))))

(define-rec
  (words-compiled! (->* ((listof named @c) int (listof int @c)) (listof int @c))
    (lambda (ws s rts)
      "Each of the listing's words whose entry is `docol`, compiled, word
       `s` on; its entry made `r-count + s`. Their tables' labels, the last
       first."
      (if (null? ws)
          rts
          (let ((w (named-value (car ws))))
            (if (and (is-kind? w k-code) (i64= (fix-val (slot-of w f-entry)) r-docol)
                     (i64<= (cells-in w f-cell0) compiled-cells-most))
                (let ((rt (label!)))
                  (begin
                    (word-compiled! w (i64->int (cells-in w f-cell0)) rt)
                    (slot-set! w f-entry (fix (i64+ r-count (int->i64 s))))
                    (words-compiled! (cdr ws) (+ s 1) (cons rt rts))))
                (words-compiled! (cdr ws) s rts)))))))

(define-type hand-code
  (subr (conv native) (maxeff (read @c) (write @c))
        ((flatarrayof i64 @c) (flatarrayof i64 @c) (flatarrayof i64 @c) (flatarrayof i64 @c)) int))

;; Instruction `w` at byte `at` of `b`'s suffix, little-endian.
(define* put4 (subr (write @heap) ((bloblet (fields) @heap) int int) unit)
  (lambda (b at w)
    (begin (bloblet-set-byte! b at (modulo w 256))
           (bloblet-set-byte! b (+ at 1) (modulo (quotient w 256) 256))
           (bloblet-set-byte! b (+ at 2) (modulo (quotient w 65536) 256))
           (bloblet-set-byte! b (+ at 3) (quotient w 16777216)))))

(define-rec
  (all-put! (->* ((bloblet (fields) @heap) (listof item @c) int (flatarrayof i64 @c)) int)
    (lambda (b xs at ls)
      "Each item placed, at instruction `at` on; the first that did not
       encode, as its place, or -1."
      (if (null? xs)
          -1
          (tagcase (car xs)
            (label-here (l) (all-put! b (cdr xs) at ls))
            (align-odd (z) (if (= (modulo at 2) 0) (begin (put4 b (* 4 at) arm-nop) (all-put! b (cdr xs) (+ at 1) ls)) (all-put! b (cdr xs) at ls)))
            (else x
              (let ((w (encoded x at ls)))
                (if (< w 0)
                    at
                    (begin (put4 b (* 4 at) w) (all-put! b (cdr xs) (+ at 1) ls))))))))))

(define-rec
  (words-table (->* ((listof int @c) (listof item @c)) (listof item @c))
    (lambda (rts acc)
      "The table of the words' tables, word 0's first (`rts` the last first)."
      (if (null? rts) acc (words-table (cdr rts) (cons (offset-of (car rts)) (cons (ins 0) acc)))))))

(define-rec
  (count-of (->* ((listof int @c) int) int) (lambda (xs n) (if (null? xs) n (count-of (cdr xs) (+ n 1))))))

(define hand-made (ref (listof hand-code @c) @c) (new nil))

(define hand-code-arm64! (->* () (sumof (made hand-code) (failed string)))
  (lambda ()
    "The machine, made once: emitted, with the listing's words compiled
     (`--compiled`), encoded, sealed. First a jump to its entry, then the
     data, then the code."
    (if (not (null? (get hand-made)))
        (sum made (car (get hand-made)))
        (begin
          (set hand-items nil) (set hand-data nil) (set hand-labels 0)
          (set l-start (label!)) (set l-entry (label!)) (set l-words (label!))
          (set h-cont -1) (set h-target -1)
          (machine!)
          (set l-materialize (label!)) (materialize! (get l-materialize))
          (let* ((cts (if (get hand-compiled) (words-compiled! (get words) 0 nil) nil))
                 (rts (if (get hand-compiled) (registers-compiled! (get register-words) (count-of cts 0) cts) cts))
                 (u (set words-compiled (count-of rts 0)))
                 (its (the (listof item @c)
                        (cons (label-here (get l-start))
                          (cons (jump j-b 0 (get l-entry))
                            (cons (ins 0)
                              (cons (label-here (get l-words))
                                (cons (ins (* 8 (count-of rts 0))) (cons (ins 0)
                                (append (words-table rts nil) (append (reverse (get hand-data)) (reverse (get hand-items))))))))))))
                 (ls (the (flatarrayof i64 @c) (make-flatarray-i64 (int->i64 (get hand-labels)) 0)))
                 (count (placed! its 0 ls))
                 (b (the (bloblet (fields) @heap) (make-bloblet (* 4 count))))
                 (bad (all-put! b its 0 ls)))
            (if (>= bad 0)
                (sum failed (string-append "tier 2: instruction " (string-append (int->string bad) " does not encode")))
                (let ((p (the hand-code (native-procedure (seal-code b)))))
                  (begin (set hand-made (list p)) (sum made p)))))))))
